# The measured population for `--cov=app`.
#
# The denominator is the code this addon ships. Three trees under `app/` are
# not that: they are the evaluation harnesses, run by hand during development
# and reached from nothing the service imports. `app/rag/keyword_filter.py`
# says so at the point where it declines to depend on one:
#
#     # Shared dir with text_match.py; defined here to avoid app/rag depending
#     # on app/evals (eval is dev-time only and shouldn't be in the runtime
#     # import graph).
#
# Each has its own `__main__.py` and is invoked as `python -m app.evals...`.
# Measured: of 142 modules under `app/`, 117 are reachable from `app.main` by
# a static walk of the import graph, and the 25 unreachable ones are exactly
# these three trees.
#
# Why they cannot stay in the denominator: 2676 statements at 33.3% dilute the
# figure that is supposed to protect the shipped code. Adding tests to an eval
# harness would raise the total, so shipped coverage could fall and the floor
# would not notice. Measured, branch-inclusive: 64.7805% over everything,
# 69.6458% over the shipped code alone.
#
# Listed one tree per line, NOT as `app/evals*/*`. That wildcard matches all
# three today (measured) and would silently swallow a fourth tree added later.
# What is excluded from a denominator is declared, so that adding to it is an
# edit somebody reviews.
#
# The claim these three lines rest on — that nothing shipped imports them — is
# not self-evident and does not stay true on its own. It is held by
# `tests/test_evals_not_in_runtime.py`, which fails if any module outside these
# trees imports one. Without that, an import added tomorrow would leave the
# exclusion here still consistent with the walk in
# `scripts/check-coverage-population.py`, and only the justification would
# become false.
[run]
omit =
    app/evals/*
    app/evals_citations/*
    app/evals_transcription/*
